  id: Scene08_FAQ_1
  speaker: WATTSON
  text: Nichrome is an alloy, a metal mixture of mostly nickel and chromium. It is
    tough, it does not rust, and it behaves very steadily in experiments like ours,
    which is exactly why school labs use a nichrome wire as the test conductor.
  ttsText: Nichrome is an alloy, a metal mixture of mostly nickel and chromium. It
